---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import profile from '../data/profile.json';

const facebook = profile.social[0];
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy · Prof. Dr. Ali Mohamed Salah"
  description="What this website does and does not collect about its visitors."
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  updated="22 October 2026"
>
  <p>
    This is the official website of Prof. Dr. Ali Mohamed Salah (Oslo, Norway). It has no accounts, no forms and no
    comments, and it does not ask you for any personal information.
  </p>

  <h2>What is collected</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Nothing by default.</strong> Fonts and images are served from this site itself, and no cookie is set until you
      choose.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Visit statistics, only if you accept.</strong> The cookie notice asks whether we may count visits. If you accept,
      the site loads Vercel Web Analytics, which counts page views, the page you came from, your country, browser and
      device type. It does not use cookies and does not follow you from site to site. If you decline, it is not loaded.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Server logs.</strong> Our host, Vercel Inc., processes your IP address and request details to deliver the
      pages and keep the site secure, as any web host does.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your choice</h2>
  <p>
    Your answer to the cookie notice is kept in your own browser (local storage, key <code>cookie-consent</code>). To change
    it, clear this site's data in your browser and the notice will appear again.
  </p>

  <h2>Other websites</h2>
  <p>
    Lecture pictures are loaded from YouTube (Google), so Google receives your IP address when you view them. Links to
    YouTube, Facebook and Amazon lead to sites with their own privacy policies; we do not control them.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Under the GDPR you may ask what is held about you, and ask for it to be corrected or deleted. Since the site holds no
    personal data beyond what its host logs, such requests usually concern Vercel. You may also complain to the Norwegian
    Data Protection Authority (Datatilsynet).
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy can be sent through the official <a href={facebook.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Facebook page</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
